   "Northwind-negotiator": "competing",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "competing"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires 24-hour regulator reporting for a broad set of incidents and prompt customer notice, but does not set a separate deadline for minor incidents. S2 keeps the 55 °C/5% limit and gives exact per-model rates to customers and regulators while barring public publication, but exceedance triggers only risk-based corrective action, not automatic sales stop. S3 sets new-unit shut-off at 24 months and a 6-year retrofit, S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months, and S5 mandates recall above 8/100k with prompt notices."
 },
